YAAP: Vegan weaponless monk


I've wanted to do this one for a long time. :)

The beginning of the game wasn't too remarkable.  I played petless,
and just went around bashing things.  Fought my way down to the
oracle level, then came back up to face the mines, with 65HP and 
an AC of -3.  I came aross a mumak in the second level of the mines,
then a gravestone, "Esk, killed by a mumak."  Esk was a wizard.
And, apart from her early demise, she'd had some luck, with some
odd boots in the pile.  Speed boots.  Yay.

Got to minetown at level 9, with little gold.  I did, however,
have 2 identify scrolls and 2 piles of orange gems.  Jacinth,
as it turned out.  Bought a few points of AC.

The bottom of the mines had a *vampire lord*.  This is not fair.
To make up for it, however, the mines also yieled a bag of holding
and an amulet of reflection.  Who needs Sokoban?

Well, I did, for the food, at least.  I'd been praying just a bit
too much for my own comfort, and I was sure Huan Ti didn't appreciate 
it.

The level below had an altar, and became my home.  Holy water
time.

On my way to Medusa, I hit a polytrap and became a red naga 
hatchling.  Boo, lost my robe.  As soon as I recovered, I proceeded
directly to the cross-aligned minetown temple and took the priest's.
Sacrificed him on his own altar and summoned Juiblex (peaceful,
as I was chaotic).

Skipped the quest, as my last monk got absolutely pasted by Master
Kaen.  Did Medusa and the Castle with a spell of levitation, no
boss liches, fortunately, but a golden naga ate my boots.

Wand was at (0:1), and I had already found charging and a magic
marker.  Replaced my speed boots, wished up a CoMR, and a wand of 
polymorph.  The wand was very productive; it immediately gave me
a +oID, +oMMissile, and another magic marker.  Had a big old
enchant-fest.  

A soldier in Ludios had a wand of death, yoink, and one zap of the
wand of poly gave me 6 Hawaiian shirts, all +0, although not for 
long.  Decided to give Croesus a miss, as I already had 10 points
intrinsic protection (3 lep halls).

Master Kaen was quite a riddle.  As I said, he'd had my previous
monk for breakfast, so I prepared lots for him.  Got up to level
30 gratis a few incubi, nurse danced(4th wish: cursed ?oGeno), and had 
my major alchemy session for the game.  I then proceeded to beat him 
to death. Boot to the head, Kaen!  Post-quest, I got sucked back down 
to level 19, gratis a vampire lord I'd cached on level 8 for that 
express purpose.

Gehennom -- An incubus had another wand of death.  I paid off
Asmodeus and Baalz due to laziness.  Juiblex wasn't there, of course.
Had quite a fight with Orcus, but it was only going to end one way.
And an Archlich summoed Yeenoghu.

Scads and scads of boss liches annoyed me, summoning MMFs which ate
my brain.  Genocide to the both of them.  Unfortunately, the MMF
had erased that particular part of my brain that remembered how
to write genocide scrolls*, so that was my 5th and final wish.
While I was at it, I took out U and ; too.  I hate them.

*My charcter's brain, that is.  I remembered that the label was
"KIRJE", but using that would have been too close to cheating for me
to be comfortable with.

Somewhere down in the pits of hell, I found a set of gauntlets of 
power, which I promptly proceeded to vaporize with an ill-thought-out
enchantment.

Whacked Rodney with a rubber chicken (not a weapon ;).  He *hounded*
me.  I've never seen him come back so many times.  Fortunately,
I had a big pile of wands of death and scrolls of charging, so he
was never much threat.  There was a cockatrice hanging around by the
upstairs on level 1, so I stoned him once more, the other 20 were
wand of death'd.

The Air plane was really difficult, even by local standards.  
Fortunately, I had my trusty wands of death at my side.  One of them
blew up when I tried to recharge it, unfortunately.

The Astral plane began with the usual "You drop the crystal ball(0:1).
The crystal ball shatters into a thousand pieces."  This plane didn't
look to be very much fun; I had grave doubts about my ability to 
fight through to hordes.  But I had thought ahead: x - a cursed
scroll of genocide.  I'd like a blessed rubber chicken, please.
The rubber chicken took care of everything except the riders.
Famine and Pestilence fell to the wands of death (although Famine
did mange to hit me twice), and the second altar was the correct
one, so I never had to face Death (although I think I probably could
have beat him up, it would be better to do so *after* the rest of the
plane is a bunch of statues).



